{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Root cause confirmed and fixed in the worktree (fix-0521-completion-material, base f147e08242f).\n\n- Hypothesis H1 (a library read inside the gate's read root sees the snapshot) was REFUTED: inside gate_session() + use_tickets_root(snapshot), config.tracker_dir() still returns the live store, and current_material_fingerprint returned the post-edit D2. The verifier's ticket tools read the snapshot only because runner.py passes cfg.tickets_path as their repo root.\n- H1' CONFIRMED: current_material_fingerprint(tid, repo_root=handle.tickets_path) returns the pre-edit D1 (5e361259eb5cc4b9) while the live store holds D2 (077a5a65ed02ed3f).\n- Fix: completion._record_read_time_material records that read-time fingerprint on the attested materialized path. transition_close.sign_completion_verdict now signs through signing._sign_manifest_under_lock with an under_lock_check (same seam plan review uses) that raises SigningError when the live material differs. Callers already map SigningError to sign_failed, so no schema change. Disposition closes and results without recorded material keep the legacy behaviour (plan step 3).\n- Red then green: 3 of 4 new tests in tests/unit/test_completion_signing_material.py failed on f147e08242f (no material recorded; signing did not refuse; record reported signed). All 4 pass. 1814 existing completion/signing/reuse tests passed; the one failure (test_completion_wrapper_duration_instrumentation) was my first draft writing material_fingerprint=None, fixed by recording only a real fingerprint, with that test unchanged.\n- make lint and make typecheck pass; make verify running."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792389084634774001,"uuid":"16bca572-9dfb-4c91-8cc7-586b71051008"}